      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The arithmetic Nagai theorem for K3^[n], generalized Kummer and the two OGrady types combines arithmetic Kuga-Satake comparisons, potentially semistable monodromy, orthogonal/spin and LLV representation theory to determine nilpotency in all even cohomological degrees. Both ell-adic and p-adic relations are the authors single main theorem; full mixed-characteristic/perfect-residue hypotheses and all source-local comparisons are retained. Other reduction-type and odd-cohomology consequences are context, not additional counts.",
